# Behavior evidence, monitoring and recovery — v1

## Status and Authority

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| Status | DOING — proposed feature definition; not approved for planning or implementation |
| Product/definition | v1; D-069 |
| Product/decision references | Constitution VII, D-020/D-021/D-065, accepted NFR-001–NFR-007 and UX refinements; D-064–D-070 |
| Author/producer | Repository definition producer |
| Specialist reviewers | QA/performance, accessibility, architecture and security/privacy review required; this feature has not been independently reviewed |
| Founder approver | Founder; feature/integrated Phase 1 acceptance not recorded |
| Created / last updated | 2026-10-04 |

The [QA/recovery contract](../../docs/phase-1-architecture/contracts/QA_RECOVERY.md)
and [acceptance matrix](../../docs/phase-1-architecture/contracts/acceptance-matrix.csv)
are canonical inputs. The [bounded amendment review](../../docs/phase-1-architecture/contracts/reviews/current-definition-amendments-2026-10-04.md)
covers their listed hashes, not this feature. Proposed process/control details
need acceptance before they become implementation expectations. The protected
prototype, documentation validators and schema fixtures are limited evidence.

## Problem, Audience, and Evidence

The founder needs trustworthy evidence that visitors can browse, explore, request
help and book, and that authorized staff can operate without false outcomes or
private-data leakage. Developers, reviewers and operators need a reproducible way
to distinguish real behavior from shape checks, mocked journeys and unsupported
readiness claims. Historical definition guards inspect wording/coverage; the
current schema fixture tests its validator, not application publication. Existing
prototype authorization and World defects remain implementation evidence, not
desired behavior or permission to fix them before the applicable gate.

## Goals and Success Measures

| Goal | Measurable outcome | Evidence source |
|---|---|---|
| Trustworthy behavior verdicts | Required outcomes are compared with approved, independently sourced oracles at the actual behavior boundary; missing evidence is explicit | Source-linked results and inspected test/fixture scope |
| Equivalent visitor journeys | Semantic and all supported stream journeys preserve essential information/help/Book, including failures | Approved scenarios exercised on the real changed surfaces |
| Truthful release/private operations | Concurrency, delayed effects and retries cannot publish an ineligible context, duplicate an operation or invent confirmation | Actual persistence/adapter and release fault evidence |
| Measured quality/recovery | Accepted targets are measured with named devices, load/cache/network profiles, timing anchors and complete verification | Performance, SLI and isolated restore evidence |
| Minimal maintainable assurance | One focused reproducing case per material behavior seam, reused fixtures, affected tests then one relevant broad batch run | Actual test scope; no count/coverage percentage target invented |

## Non-Goals and Protected Scope

- No tests merely asserting documentation phrases, row counts or implementation-
  copied expected results. Necessary artifact integrity is reported separately.
- No production readiness, accessibility, legal/vendor compliance or graph
  acceptance inferred from a validator, mocked API, desktop-only result or `/health`.
- No new test runner, monitoring vendor, deployment provider, cloud region, paid
  activation, provisioned environment or automatic incident recipient selected.
- No mutation of production/shared data, live load/fault injection, migrations,
  credentials, external messages, commits or deployment authorized by this draft.
- Do not change the accepted product to make a test pass, silently omit required
  failures, lower targets, switch the session stream or replace a provider.

## User Journeys and Failure Journeys

### Primary journey

1. Identify the approved requirement, current source revision and relevant actual
   behavior boundary; record assumptions and incomplete contracts explicitly.
2. Reproduce a meaningful failure with a focused synthetic fixture in an approved
   isolated environment, using an independently justified expected outcome.
3. Exercise actual state/requests/persistence, including relevant denial, boundary,
   concurrency and recovery cases. Controlled external fixtures have stated limits.
4. Run affected tests and the relevant broad suite once per coherent batch when
   practical, then inspect changed browser surfaces against approved scenarios.
5. Present the actual results, evidence limits and unresolved inputs for the
   required independent review and founder acceptance; do not promote a candidate
   solely because a command is green.

### Accessibility and non-WebGL equivalent

Verify complete semantic HTML before JavaScript, supported Quick Access processes,
keyboard/touch/pointer alternatives, focus/zoom, reduced motion, meaningful media
alternatives and four-stream parity. Automated accessibility checks support manual
keyboard and assistive-technology process evidence; they cannot replace it.

### Failure and recovery

Force relevant failures before writes, after external receipt, before acknowledgement,
after durable recording and during reconciliation/restart. Preserve operation
identity and authoritative private truth. Missing/deferred provider capability
evidence stays incomplete. Restore only into an approved isolated quarantine and
enforce retained deletion/expiry/withdrawal decisions before any serving claim.

## Functional Requirements

These feature-local bindings refine the acceptance matrix; they are not new approvals.

| ID | Requirement | Priority | Verification |
|---|---|---|---|
| FQA-01 | Bind each behavior verdict to an approved oracle, actual boundary, inspected fixture/test scope, source identity and relevant runtime versions; label unsupported/missing evidence explicitly | Must | Evidence and oracle inspection against actual execution |
| FQA-02 | Separate unit, schema/contract, real database/adapter integration, browser and manual accessibility evidence; exercise negative/boundary/concurrency cases where material | Must | Actual layer scope, fixture isolation and representative failures |
| FQA-03 | Use reusable focused fixtures, affected tests and one practical relevant broad run per coherent batch; repeat broader runs only for concrete changes/failures | Must | Batch execution evidence and reason for any repetition |
| FQA-04 | Exercise QA-SEMANTIC/QA-STREAM at real visitor surfaces, with no-JS HTML, accepted Apply/precedence, scripting failures, permitted context survival and essential process parity | Must | Browser/HTML evidence tied to accepted references and predicates |
| FQA-05 | Exercise QA-SPATIAL/QA-AUDIO on the same coherent model and actual runtime: safe ground, reversal, loss/cancellation, resource ownership, optional sound and silent recovery | Must | Named-device scene/input/network/playback and three-view evidence |
| FQA-06 | Exercise QA-PUBLICATION across real preparation/eligibility/cutover boundaries, including mixed/stale generations, unknown outcomes, withdrawal, warm caches and eligible rollback | Must | Concurrent/fault results and authoritative routed/release identities |
| FQA-07 | Exercise QA-IDENTITY/QA-PRIVACY/QA-AI for server role/object/purpose denial, consent/retention/deletion, approved grounding/data routes, injection refusal and outage recovery | Must | Actual protected boundaries and required independent legal/provider evidence |
| FQA-08 | Exercise QA-BOOKING/QA-HANDOFF for qualification/email/slot/owner eligibility, current availability, consent, assignment, daylight-saving boundaries, uncertain writes and no duplicate/guessed outcomes | Must | Actual lineage/persistence/adapter and controlled concurrency cases |
| FQA-09 | Exercise QA-PERFORMANCE/QA-RECOVERY against preserved accepted targets, named supported clients and isolated timed recovery; absent device/SLI/retention mechanisms cannot pass | Must | Complete profile, load/integrity, availability accounting and restore verification |
| FQA-10 | Monitor the defined public/API/AI/booking-entry outcomes with approved SLI accounting; distinguish dependency, stale/unknown measurement and business-operation failures from mere process uptime | Must | Approved numerator/denominator/exclusions/source and breach detection cases |
| FQA-11 | Restrict diagnostic/alert access and recipients by approved purpose/grants; redact secrets and private context, avoid movement histories/device fingerprints and do not invent mailbox ownership | Must | Network/log/storage and access-denial evidence with actual approved recipients |
| FQA-12 | Keep artifact integrity, schema-only and mocked frontend evidence separate from product verdicts; report exact gaps and require independent review/approval before the applicable release gate | Must | Evidence classification and concrete acceptance inspection |

## Non-Functional Requirements

Targets below are existing approved constraints, not observed results.

| ID | Area | Measurable target | Verification |
|---|---|---|---|
| FQA-N01 | Semantic performance | Quick Access p75 LCP ≤2.5 s, INP ≤200 ms, CLS ≤0.1 on the approved profile | Lab and field-ready evidence; optional 3D cannot regress the semantic path |
| FQA-N02 | Optional 3D transfer | Initial ≤8 MB desktop / ≤4 MB mobile; incremental room ≤5 MB / ≤2.5 MB at defined cache state | Complete compressed manifests and actual network transfer |
| FQA-N03 | Capacity/integrity | 25 concurrent visitors and three simultaneous chats on a repeatable representative browse/chat/booking-entry profile | Completed flows without integrity error/unhandled failure |
| FQA-N04 | Availability | 99.9% monthly public-site, API and AI/booking-entry target | Approved SLI numerator/denominator/exclusions/source; unknown data is not fabricated uptime |
| FQA-N05 | Recovery | RPO ≤24 h and RTO ≤8 h; both remain explicit adequacy/reassessment risks | Approved timing anchors and isolated recovery including verification before serving |
| FQA-N06 | Browser/accessibility | Latest two stable evergreen families at dated QA; Safari/iOS 16.4 floor; accepted WCAG 2.2 AA target over complete applicable pages/processes | Exact-version desktop/mobile and manual assistive-technology evidence |
| FQA-N07 | Device envelope | Approved NFR-007 numerical frame-time, memory and thermal/degradation limits required before 3D implementation; values are still held | Named-device measurement methods and accepted thresholds; no inherited FPS |
| FQA-N08 | Diagnostic privacy | No secret/private transcript or new precise movement/fingerprint collection under this feature; exact evidence retention and access are approved inputs | Actual telemetry/storage/redaction and permission inspection |

### Proposed device-measurement method

This method refines FQA-N01/02/03/07 and the existing QA contract. It remains
producer definition, not accepted numerical limits or a benchmark result. Freeze
the profile, timing/accounting anchors and pass/fail inputs before collection;
do not choose them afterward to make observed results pass.

| Evidence dimension | Required profile/observation | Limit of the conclusion |
|---|---|---|
| Client identity | Non-unique QA model/CPU/GPU/RAM class, OS/browser/tool versions, actual renderer, viewport/pixel ratio/refresh rate and physical versus emulated execution | Named lab hardware only; no visitor fingerprint, serial, account or persistent device identifier |
| Run conditions | Source/release/assets, delivery stream, cache/storage state, actual network or explicit simulation, power mode, background load, warm-up/duration/repetitions and collection overhead | Exact values/sample method need review; no unrecorded fast-network, short-session or quiet-machine substitution |
| Transfer | Record raw octets, encoded payload, transport size, decoded body, cache visibility and asset dependencies; identify initial entry, room, prefetch, shared and optional-audio attribution | Headers/retries/cache can change measured transport; hidden cross-origin timing is unknown, not a free asset |
| Frame behavior | Record trace/sampling method, foreground interval, frame-time distribution, dropped/partially presented frames where available, interaction/loading stalls and context loss | Callback intervals and average FPS alone do not prove presented-frame or device-tier compliance |
| Memory/resources | Separate JS heap, process memory, actual renderer resource counts and labelled estimates of geometry/texture/render-target allocation; compare repeated entry/reversal/eviction/exit | Download bytes, heap or object counts cannot certify exact GPU memory; shared ownership and collection timing remain explicit |
| Sustained behavior | Compare defined initial and sustained traversal phases under recorded power/ambient conditions; report deterioration, visible safe recovery and unavailable sensors | Emulation/throttling is a controlled condition, not measured physical-phone thermals; absent readings stay unknown |
| Behavior under load | Exercise accepted representative journeys with 25 concurrent visitors/three chats and failures, including preserved operation truth | Throughput or a static health result cannot replace completed correct processes; no live/shared target is authorized |

Declare cold/warm behavior and deduplication/attribution before the run. Count
actual requests as well as declared asset bytes; early prefetch cannot hide room
cost by moving it outside the chosen interval. Report compressed payload and
transport totals separately and reconcile them against the asset manifest.
Preserve accepted caps; report raw bytes plus MB and MiB until the unit/accounting
interpretation is accepted. Do not silently select a more convenient interpretation.
[Resource Timing](https://www.w3.org/TR/resource-timing/) and its
[transfer-size documentation](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/PerformanceResourceTiming/transferSize)
distinguish body/transport and restricted timing; a zero reading alone cannot prove
zero network cost. Frame evidence can use the actual client's reviewed trace
facilities, such as [Chrome's frame analysis](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/devtools/performance/reference).

Context7 `/microsoft/playwright.dev` and [official emulation documentation](https://playwright.dev/docs/emulation)
were checked 2026-10-04: emulation changes browser parameters, not the host's
physical GPU/thermal hardware. Thus a mobile viewport on this Windows host remains
desktop/emulated evidence. Local read-only discovery found an i3-1115G4, Intel UHD
Graphics and approximately 19.8 GiB physical RAM on Windows 11; browser/rendering,
power and performance were not measured. This is an available lab candidate, not
a selected production floor. Physical-phone access is requested and remains held.
Actual real-device methods and NFR-007 limits need specialist review and acceptance;
no tool installation, instrumentation, stress test or telemetry collection is granted.

## SEO and Publication Requirements

Test the accepted foundation's meaningful no-JS HTML, eligible metadata/canonicals,
structured data matching visible facts, internal links, sitemap/robots exclusions,
retirement/redirects and draft isolation. The public derivatives must correspond
to the same eligible approved release; immutable checksums alone do not grant
eligibility. A schema guard or crawled placeholder cannot establish publication
or complete SEO readiness. This feature publishes no evidence dashboard or claims.

## Data, Privacy, and Security

| Data/actor | Classification | Purpose/consent | Retention/deletion | Access/control | Region/provider |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Synthetic fixtures | Isolated non-client test data | Approved reproducible boundary verification | Approved test lifecycle; no implicit production copy | Explicitly verified test target/permissions | Native local operation supported; environment provisioning separate |
| Diagnostic/performance evidence | Potentially private operational data | Minimal permitted assurance/incident purpose | Exact classification/retention/deletion mappings remain held | Purpose-bound review/operator access; redaction before disclosure | No new data route or monitoring provider selected |
| Private process/provider/audit records | Existing canonical classes | Approved process purpose/consent only | Class-specific clock/deletion/backup/provider obligations; not blanket 90 days | Server grants/object scope; no admin-universal read | Approved identity/AI policies retained; capabilities independently verified |
| Aggregate availability/load measurement | Approved minimal measurement policy | Defined operational quality accounting | Approved policy, not permanent unreviewed telemetry | Bounded approved observation/alerts | Cloud/provider/cost planning deferred |

Inspect fixtures before database-writing tests; neither a `pytest` command nor
SQLite-only results prove isolated PostgreSQL behavior. Wrong-role/object, revoked
grants, CSRF/session failures, self-approval, expiry and restored deleted data must
be tested at real boundaries when implemented. Dedicated privacy/security alias
ownership remains undecided; monitoring infrastructure cannot assign it by default.

## AI and Human-Handoff Requirements

Evaluate source/release matching, supported versus unsupported answers, approved
classification/provider routing, refusal, injection and safe outages. Code/mock
results cannot prove a vendor's no-training/residency agreement. Handoff evidence
must include stale/unknown presence, consent refusal and current assignment;
Teams alerts are not accepted human requests or booking confirmations. Separate
consented human media from decorative ambience and verify its required alternatives.

## Interfaces and Data Contracts

| Contract | Producer/consumer | Compatibility | Idempotency/recovery |
|---|---|---|---|
| Acceptance matrix and approved requirements | Product authorities → tests/reviewers | Preserve each required boundary and approved target | Missing/unexecuted evidence stays pending |
| Publication/data/security/process catalogues | Canonical process owners → integration verification | Exact accepted schemas/grants and source/operation identities | Safe retries, uncertain effects and authoritative state; no fabricated confirmation |
| Device/browser/SLI profile | Performance/operations authorities → measurements | Recorded actual clients, cache/network/load assumptions and SLI accounting | Invalid/unknown samples cannot silently certify a target |
| Backup/restore/deletion contract | Durable process owners → isolated recovery | Eligible release and retained deletion/withdrawal decisions | Quarantine and verify before serving; recovery includes reconciliation |

No new endpoint, database schema, external event or deployment resource is selected.
Key concepts are approved oracle, behavior boundary, controlled fixture, scoped
evidence, measurement profile, unresolved operation and eligible recovery candidate.

## Technology Constraints

Use approved families and framework-supported testing patterns during the later
accepted plan. Exact test/browser/driver/tool versions must join the latest
mutually compatible stable graph; a version printed by a test is evidence, not
stack selection. Docker is not required locally. Deployment and cost planning
remain deferred with Azure/AWS candidates; Outlook/Teams needs no blanket
Microsoft 365 setup. Retained Entra and personal/confidential AI data-route policy
is not replaced by that hosting deferral.

## Acceptance Scenarios

1. **Given** a passing phrase/hash/schema check, **when** evidence is classified,
   **then** it proves only its inspected artifact/validator boundary, not runtime,
   authorization, accessibility or publication behavior.
2. **Given** an invalid approved-contract input accepted by the application but
   rejected by a local schema fixture, **when** the actual request/persistence
   boundary is exercised, **then** acceptance remains unresolved until that
   boundary rejects it before prohibited persistence/effects. Do not substitute
   the fixture's green result for the real failure.
3. **Given** a wrong role/object, revoked grant or combined-role self-approval,
   **when** an actual protected mutation/read is attempted, **then** current server
   authorization denies it without disclosing unauthorized private context.
4. **Given** a controlled missing acknowledgement after an external effect,
   **when** retry/reconciliation runs, **then** the operation identity is preserved,
   no duplicate effect is created and pending does not become guessed confirmation.
5. **Given** interleaved publication generations and stale late responses,
   **when** cutover/withdrawal/rollback occurs, **then** only eligible coherent
   public context is served and private booking/handoff truth survives unchanged.
6. **Given** disabled JavaScript/WebGL, constrained stream or failed transaction
   scripting, **when** the visitor browses and requests help/Book, **then** the
   approved equivalent semantic process is verified or its concrete gap reported.
7. **Given** keyboard/touch, reduced motion, magnification or assistive technology,
   **when** the complete supported process is exercised, **then** focus, controls,
   content and alternatives meet their approved criteria; axe alone cannot pass it.
8. **Given** real movement/reversal and delayed/corrupt/mismatched area loading,
   **when** safe boundaries and eviction/exit are exercised, **then** actual ground,
   resource ownership, Stop/recovery and permitted process preservation are proved.
9. **Given** optional ambience never enabled, muted, failed or withdrawn, **when**
   the actual browser journey is inspected, **then** optional fetch/playback and
   essential process behavior follow the accepted policy without fake staff activity.
10. **Given** the approved named-client/cache/network/load profile, **when** capacity
    and performance are measured, **then** recorded results cover accepted targets
    and integrity outcomes; a desktop probe cannot certify an untested phone tier.
11. **Given** incomplete/stale observation or a health response without business
    dependency proof, **when** monthly SLI/breach state is assessed, **then** the
    approved accounting distinguishes missing evidence and business failures;
    unknown measurements cannot be manufactured as successful uptime.
12. **Given** a backup predating deletion, expiry, withdrawal or a resolved external
    operation, **when** isolated quarantine recovery runs, **then** retained
    authoritative suppression/reconciliation is enforced before serving, with
    measured RPO/RTO including verification. Process startup alone cannot pass.
13. **Given** diagnostic/alert configuration that would leak secrets, private
    context or precise movement, **when** its real IO/access is inspected, **then**
    the prohibited collection/disclosure is rejected and evidence stays scoped.
    No undefined email owner or unauthorized external alert is invented.
14. **Given** controlled approved knowledge and a current eligible publication,
    **when** guidance is requested at the actual answer/source boundary, **then**
    supported answers cite the matching approved accessible sources. Unsupported,
    withdrawn or mismatched evidence and injected requests to invent commitments
    cannot justify substantive guidance or authorize booking, tool action or
    publication; verify truthful refusal/cannot-verify and independent help/Book.
15. **Given** synthetic inputs covering permitted, unknown, unmapped and prohibited
    data classes, **when** the real policy/adapter boundary processes them, **then**
    only the approved verified route receives permitted data. Denied classes or
    an unavailable required route do not silently fall back to another provider.
    A controlled outage preserves truthful recovery; mocked routing cannot prove
    vendor residency, no-training terms or operational entitlement.
16. **Given** the BF-01 six qualification fields, purpose-specific consent and
    optional budget, **when** the real booking lineage is exercised, **then** no
    required account, name, phone, upload or prior AI interaction is introduced.
    Invalid/incomplete qualification, forged/replayed/expired email verification
    and corrected email cannot enable slots under the former challenge. A current
    verified challenge permits only eligible owners and actual 30-minute slots;
    visitor-local daylight-saving display preserves the slot's unambiguous instant
    and timezone. Missing slots/owners provide truthful recovery. Submission stays
    pending until the approved calendar/meeting and local state reconcile; apply
    scenario 4 to unknown effects. Exact challenge/provider rules remain held.
17. **Given** current available staff, stale/unknown/offline availability, consent
    refusal or an ineligible assignment, **when** the actual assistance process
    requests human handoff, **then** only current eligible assignment plus explicit
    consent permits the approved context transfer. Refusal forbids that transfer;
    unavailable/unknown states offer honest Contact/Book recovery without an
    invented response promise. A Teams alert cannot certify human acceptance or
    booking confirmation. Test the actual expiry/revocation boundary once defined.
18. **Given** a database-writing, load or fault test with an unverified/shared
    target, insufficient approved scope or fixtures pointing outside isolation,
    **when** execution is prepared, **then** it stops before those effects and
    identifies the missing target/scope evidence without exposing credentials.
    With the explicitly approved isolated target and inspected reusable fixtures,
    verify actual permitted persistence behavior. SQLite-only or mocked results
    remain limited to that boundary and cannot pass PostgreSQL integration.
19. **Given** controlled expired/revoked sessions, cross-site write attempts,
    non-consented guidance or mapped retention-clock boundaries, **when** actual
    identity and persistence behavior is exercised, **then** approved session/CSRF
    enforcement denies prohibited operations, refused retention leaves no hidden
    durable transcript and mapped expiry is enforced without resetting its clock.
    Verify permitted controls as well as denials; exact identity/retention inputs
    and vendor copies stay held, with restore suppression covered by scenario 12.

## Dependencies and Manual Inputs

| Dependency/input | Owner | Needed by | Blocking behavior |
|---|---|---|---|
| Approved UI/3D references and executable behavior | Feature owners/reviewers/founder | Runtime/browser verification | A board or protected prototype cannot substitute for the required implementation |
| Exact schemas, identity/grants and external operation contracts | Canonical contract owners | Integration/concurrency/denial cases | Logical fields or mocks cannot freeze vendor truth or permissions |
| Device/load/cache/network profiles and numerical envelope | Performance/3D reviewers/founder | Measurement acceptance | No fabricated thresholds, targets or untested-client certification |
| SLI accounting, diagnostic policy and authorized operational recipients | Operations/security/privacy owners | Monitoring/alert implementation | No unapproved exclusions, retention, collection or mailbox assignment |
| Recovery/backup/deletion/provider reconciliation contracts | Operations and canonical private-process owners | Isolated restore evidence | Startup-only or privacy-unsafe restoration cannot pass |
| Approved isolated test environment and operation scope | Founder and relevant data/security owners | Executing mutations/fault/load tests | This specification grants no infrastructure/data/provider permission |
| Independent feature review and integrated Phase 1 acceptance | Nonproducer reviewers/founder | Planning/implementation | New producer draft remains unreviewed; other hashes do not cover it |

## Open Decisions and Assumptions

| Item | Type | Material impact | Proposed default | Approval required |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Measurement/SLI/recovery anchors and device limits | Evidence/decision | Validity of quality and breach verdicts | Preserve existing targets; hold unmeasured profiles/mechanisms | Reviewed operational and numerical contracts |
| Diagnostic classification/retention, alert recipients and environment permission | Decision | Private data and external effects | Minimal synthetic/local inspection only until explicit policy/scope exists | Data/security/founder approval; alias ownership remains undecided |
| Provider capability and deployment choice | Held input | Real fencing/reconciliation/recovery proof | Provider-independent obligations; no deployment planning now | D-068 deferral retained; later specific proof/approval |
| Evidence accounting | Assumption | Prevents inflated readiness | Report actual boundary and limitations rather than check counts | Existing founder testing policy retained |

## Review and Approval

Quality checklist and specialist/SEO/accessibility/security/privacy review are
required. This producer specification is not an executed test suite, monitoring
system or readiness verdict. No approved plan or executable tasks exist; complete
feature and Phase 1 acceptance precede implementation.

